  "worked_solution": "From the given repeated integral, we see that $R$ can be written as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le y,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le {y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe wish to rewrite our triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\u222d}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(x)}^{{v}_{2}(x)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,y)}^{{u}_{2}(x,y)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nSince both repeated integrals first integrate with respect to $z,$ the $z$-limits remain the same as before:\n\n$$\n{\u222d}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(x)}^{{v}_{2}(x)}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072974/assets/a89646433c8851f66c94092b75fae7b46b01f31c69ca03d338464b87bd7f5df4.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is a type II region in the $xy$-plane:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le y}\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$ to $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x,$ we write $D$ as a type I region.\n\nNotice that the bottom boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is \n\n$$\nx=y\\,\u27f9\\,y=x\n$$\n\nand the top boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=1.\n$$\n\nThen, the type I representation of the region $D$ is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,x\\le y\\le 1},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072974/assets/1604e44050208cfb3b4dd81d35bff9769c7498d8304583d5ba92ad4b2f62fd05.png)\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\u222d}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$",
